nes":true,"primarySubtitle":"1.8.0","secondarySubtitle":"Tue Sep 15 2026 07:05:52 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)"},{"$kind":"TitledParagraph","text":"- Bug fixes and performance improvements.\n\nNote: This is the last version to support iOS 14. Future updates will require iOS 15 or later.","style":"detail","wantsCollapsedNewlines":true,"primarySubtitle":"1.7.0","secondarySubtitle":"Sun Aug 16 2026 02:24:36 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)"},{"$kind":"TitledParagraph","text":"- Add support for AnyTLS proxy protocol.\n- Bug fixes and other minor improvements.","style":"detail","wantsCollapsedNewlines":true,"primarySubtitle":"1.6.0","secondarySubtitle":"Thu May 21 2026 02:17:03 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)"},{"$kind":"TitledParagraph","text":"- Add support for Reality TLS (https://github.com/XTLS/REALITY).\n- Bug fixes and other minor improvements.","style":"detail","wantsCollapsedNewlines":true,"primarySubtitle":"1.5.5","secondarySubtitle":"Wed Jan 14 2026 00:08:47 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)"},{"$kind":"TitledParagraph","text":"- Optimized for iOS 26 with improved reliability and performance.\n- Bug fixes and other minor improvements.","style":"detail","wantsCollapsedNewlines":true,"primarySubtitle":"1.5.4","secondarySubtitle":"Mon Oct 20 2025 13:33:36 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)"},{"$kind":"TitledParagraph","text":"- Optimized for iOS 26 with improved reliability and performance.\n- Bug fixes and other minor improvements.","style":"detail","wantsCollapsedNewlines":true,"primarySubtitle":"1.5.3","secondarySubtitle":"Thu Sep 11 2025 12:22:32 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)"},{"$kind":"TitledParagraph","text":"- Adds jqlang(https://github.com/jqlang/jq) for HTTP(S) rewrite to handle HTTP(S) JSON body modification.\n- Bug fixes and other minor improvements.","style":"detail","wantsCollapsedNewlines":true,"primarySubtitle":"1.5.2","secondarySubtitle":"Fri Jul 18 2025 19:03:42 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)"},{"$kind":"TitledParagraph","text":"- Supports 2022-blake3-aes-128-gcm and 2022-blake3-aes-256-gcm for shadowsocks protocol.\n- Bug fixes and other minor improvements.","style":"detail","wantsCollapsedNewlines":true,"primarySubtitle":"1.5.1","secondarySubtitle":"Tue May 06 2025 18:38:52 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)"},{"$kind":"TitledParagraph","text":"- Supports VLESS proxy protocol.\n- Bug fixes and other minor improvements.","style":"detail","wantsCollapsedNewlines":true,"primarySubtitle":"1.5.0","secondarySubtitle":"Sun Apr 21 2024 17:39:47 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)"},{"$kind":"TitledParagraph","text":"- Bug fixes and other minor improvements.","style":"detail","wantsCollapsedNewlines":true,"primarySubtitle":"1.4.2","secondarySubtitle":"Thu Nov 02 2023 16:53:20 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)"},{"$kind":"TitledParagraph","text":"- Fixes an issue related to SSR proxy protocol.","style":"detail","wantsCollapsedNewlines":true,"primarySubtitle":"1.4.1","secondarySubtitle":"Thu Sep 28 2023 11:29:07 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)"},{"$kind":"TitledParagraph","text":"- Supports sharing configuration to Quantumult X running on Apple TV (tvOS 17.0+) through iCloud.\n- Fixes iOS 17.0 compatibility issues.\n- Bug fixes and other minor improvements.","style":"detail","wantsCollapsedNewlines":true,"primarySubtitle":"1.4.0","secondarySubtitle":"Wed Sep 13 2023 05:59:38 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)"},{"$kind":"TitledParagraph","text":"- Adds an option \"enhanced_compatibility_ssid_list\" in [general] section, this SSID specific option will be considered only when the global option 「Enhanced Compatibility」is Off.\n- Bug fixes and other minor improvements.","style":"detail","wantsCollapsedNewlines":true,"primarySubtitle":"1.3.0","secondarySubtitle":"Sat Mar 25 2023 20:22:34 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)"},{"$kind":"TitledParagraph","text":"- The rewrite module now supports evaluting both HTTP(S) URL and headers (new keyword \"url-and-header\"). Please view sample configuraiton in app for details.\n- Add obfs \"shadowsocks-http\" and \"vmess-http\" to distinguish the two different http obfuscations (Shadowsocks and VMess). This is useful when you deployed a Shadowsocks service combined with VMess http obfuscation using VMess related server (V2Ray or others).\n- Add TLS option tls-no-session-ticket and tls-no-session-reuse for TLS based proxy protocols for specific use cases for some users.\n- Bug fixes and other minor improvements.","style":"detail","wantsCollapsedNewlines":true,"primarySubtitle":"1.2.0","secondarySubtitle":"Mon Dec 19 2022 16:21:53 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)"},{"$kind":"TitledParagraph","text":"- Fixes iOS 16 compatibility issues.\n- Bug fixes and other minor improvements.","style":"detail","wantsCollapsedNewlines":true,"primarySubtitle":"1.1.0","secondarySubtitle":"Sat Oct 08 2022 10:03:02 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)"},{"$kind":"TitledParagraph","text":"- Bug fixes and other minor improvements.","style":"detail","wantsCollapsedNewlines":true,"primarySubtitle":"1.0.32","secondarySubtitle":"Fri Aug 26 2022 22:57:44 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)"},{"$kind":"TitledParagraph","text":"- When DoQ (DNS over QUIC) and DoH (DNS over HTTPS) are both set, the DNS request will be sent to all of them simultaneously.\n- Add new params circumvent-ipv4-answer and circumvent-ipv6-answer for DNS configuration to ignore the DNS answers that you don't want to use, like 127.0.0.1 or 0.0.0.0. This is useful when you configured multiple DNS servers, and some of them replied with spoofing results.\n- Add new param tls-alpn for TLS based proxies to customize the ALPN (Application-Layer Protocol Negotiation ) when the TLS handshake is initiated.\n- Add new type host-wildcard for filter rules, the wildcard * and ? can be used. The already existed host and host-suffix type rules are always recommended for better perfomance.\n- Bug fixes and other minor improvements.","style":"detail","wantsCollapsedNewlines":true,"primarySubtitle":"1.0.31","secondarySubtitle":"Fri Aug 19 2022 23:18:07 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)"},{"$kind":"TitledParagraph","text":"- Supports DoQ (DNS over QUIC).\n- Supports HTTP/3 for DoH (DNS over HTTPS).\n- The reject rule behavior (DNS layer) can be adjusted to \"no error no answer\" response or \"NXDOMAIN\" response instead of the default loopback IP response.\n- Bug fixes and other minor improvements.","style":"detail","wantsCollapsedNewlines":true,"primarySubtitle":"1.0.30","secondarySubtitle":"Sun Jul 03 2022 01:10:50 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)"},{"$kind":"TitledParagraph","text":"- Supports multiple DoH (DNS over HTTPS).\n- Supports SOCKS5 (over TLS) proxy protocol.\n- Supports UDP over TCP transport for UDP packets via shadowsocks protocol (this feature is only compatible with server side deplopyed by ssr Python version).\n- Fixes an issue related to HTTP deflate encoding.\n- Bug fixes and other minor improvements.","style":"detail","wantsCollapsedNewlines":true,"primarySubtitle":"1.0.29","secondarySubtitle":"Fri May 20 2022 10:15:07 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)"},{"$kind":"TitledParagraph","text":"- Supports WebSocket for proxy protocol Trojan.\n- Adds new option alive-checking for url-latency-benchmark policy.\n- Adds new option multi-interface-balance for filter rule to load-balance traffic on different network interfaces.\n- Bug fixes and other minor improvements.","style":"detail","wantsCollapsedNewlines":true,"primarySubtitle":"1.0.28","secondarySubtitle":"Sun Mar 27 2022 13:29:37 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)"},{"$kind":"TitledParagraph","text":"- Supports AEAD (Header) for proxy protocol VMess.\n- Supports UDP relay (UDP over TCP) for proxy protocol VMess.\n- Supports UDP relay (UDP over TCP) for proxy protocol Trojan.\n- Supports filter rule with new option via-interface (eg: via-interface=en1) to easily split up traffic on different interfaces (mainly for M1 chip Mac users).\n- Bug fixes and other minor improvements.","style":"detail","wantsCollapsedNewlines":true,"primarySubtitle":"1.0.27","secondarySubtitle":"Sat Jan 15 2022 19:44:14 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)"},{"$kind":"TitledParagraph","text":"- Fixed a crash that could occur on iPad with keyboard or pencil connected.","style":"detail","wantsCollapsedNewlines":true,"primarySubtitle":"1.0.26","secondarySubtitle":"Wed Oct 20 2021 01:45:46 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)"},{"$kind":"TitledParagraph","text":"- Adds additional params for filter rules to customize outbound interfaces. Please view sample configuraiton in app for details.\n- Bug fixes and other minor improvements.","style":"detail","wantsCollapsedNewlines":true,"primarySubtitle":"1.0.25","secondarySubtitle":"Fri Oct 15 2021 22:20:04 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)"},{"$kind":"TitledParagraph","text":"- Adds option \"doh_user_agent\" for customized DoH request header field \"User-Agent\", please view sample configuraiton (section \"[general]\") in app for details.\n- The option \"excluded_ssids\" can be deployed with the DoH settings, please view sample configuraiton (section \"[dns]\") in app for details.\n- Adds new type of proxy policy \"dest-hash\".\n- Bug fixes and other minor improvements.","style":"detail","wantsCollapsedNewlines":true,"primarySubtitle":"1.0.24","secondarySubtitle":"Thu Aug 12 2021 23:50:16 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)"},{"$kind":"TitledParagraph","text":"- Adds DNS over HTTPS(DoH) support, view sample configuraiton in app for details.\n- Bug fixes and other minor improvements.","style":"detail","wantsCollapsedNewlines":true,"primarySubtitle":"1.0.23","secondarySubtitle":"Mon Jul 05 2021 15:13:29 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)"}],"url":null,"mergeWhenFetched":false,"fetchStrategy":"onPageLoad","batchGroup":null,"seeAllAction":null,"footerTitle":null,"footerAction":null,"eyebrow":null,"eyebrowArtwork":null,"footerStyle":null,"titleArtwork":null,"subtitle":n